YHWH Ya' Way — v0.1.0  (Kobo/e-reader presentation overhaul + reader targeting)
=================================================

The semantic-version line above (first non-blank line) is read by the build
scripts (dev/build_dmg.sh, dev/installer.iss, dev/build_appimage.sh) and by
dev/generate_appcast.py. Everything below is human-readable metadata.

Versioning (set 2026-06-07): pre-final releases are v0.0.x and v0.1.x …;
the first full release will be v1.0.0 (then v1.0.x patches, v1.1.x big updates,
and v2.0.0 a complete overhaul). The former "v1.0.0-beta.N" naming is RETIRED.

v0.1.0 ships the e-reader presentation overhaul proven on a real Kobo across
three device-QA rounds: per-book title pages on their own spine files (the only
page break e-ink kepub honors), badge popups with plain-text separators that
survive Kobo's Footnote preview, verse-end badge placement (no more
chapter-start spill), centered chapter numerals, embedded Ge'ez TTF + original-
script popups, reader targeting in the wizard ("Where will you read it?"),
the 83-book library card, one Colophon, and the Kobo font pack as a companion
download. Live corpus/edition/test counts and the roadmap live in
dev/SESSION_STATE.md + dev/CHANGELOG.md (not this file).
